// REQUIRES: long
// P03.26: unsafe.Sizeof, Alignof and Offsetof of types nested by value (10000 levels of every shape: structs, arrays, generic instances, an array with a pointer back, structs and arrays declared top down too, so a size is asked before the parts are declared, and a dag of 30 levels = 2^30 leaves).
// The sizes were worked out by a recursion that stopped at depth 64 and
// answered one word below it; they are now worked out with a stack of their
// own and a memo for every type (Checker::gcLayout), so there is no limit on
// the depth and a type that is used twice (`dag`) is worked out once. The
// numbers come from a model of the gc layout in Inputs/check-sizeof-nest.py,
// which sizeof-nest-go.long.test compares with `go run`.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-sizeof-nest.py %gopp %t.d deep-struct,array,generic,wide,dag
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-sizeof-nest.py %gopp %t.d rev-struct,array
